{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For I have known him.</b> This proves it directly." "<b>To the end that he may command his children.</b> All this the blessed El said and did in order that Abraham, upon seeing the greatness of His kindnesses even toward the wicked and His judgments against those who do not repent, may command his children — so that they keep <b>to do righteousness and justice</b>." "<b>To the end that YHWH may bring upon Abraham that which He has spoken concerning him.</b> The ultimate end intended by the blessed El in all this was to bring upon Abraham that which He had spoken, as He said: לִהְיוֹת לְךָ לֵאלֹהִים וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ (Genesis 17:7)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:36.914702547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}